<title>UK: Goldman, UBS place UK govt stakes in power groups.</title>
<headline>Goldman, UBS place UK govt stakes in power groups.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UBS and Goldman Sachs were on Tuesday involved in placing large UK government holdings in British power companies Powergen, National Power and Southern Electric, London traders said.</p>
<p>UBS was reported to have placed around 21 million shares in PowerGen, later confirmed as 17 million shares by sources close to the brokerage at 498p per share.</p>
<p>Goldman were said to have placed around 28 million National Power shares at 393p perim share and around 900,000 shares in Southern Electric at 650p.  </p>
<p>No-one at Goldman Sachs or UBS were immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
